  "extras": [],
  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What does Xargatha's Stone Gaze affect and not affect?",
      "answer": "It prevents “movement actions”, that is, selecting the movement option when resolving a card:\n• ❌ They can’t use a normal movement action to move.\n• ❌ They can’t use a movement action to fast travel (which chooses, then replaces, a movement action).\n• ✅ They can use a “place” or “swap” effect (such as Arien’s Alt Blue).\n• ✅ They can be pushed or moved by another effect (if the effect ignores immunity).\n• ✅ They can take another action type that involves movement (such as Brogan’s Primary Red) or a Fast Travel (Silverarrow’s Gold).",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "Does Xargatha's Constrict affect heavy minions as well?",
      "answer": "No. Initially you can only kill melee minions, but on Tier 3 you can get melee or ranged minions, but never the heavy minion.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "Does my effect trigger next round?",
      "answer": "No. Active effects always “clear” at the end of the round: A “next turn” effect played on Turn 4 will not carry over to the next round.",
      "source": "goa2-faq (common)"
    }
  ],
  "lore": "Xargatha was the high priestess of the sacred shrine when it was desecrated and the holy relic was stolen. Her anger and grief were so powerful that they’ve changed her into a monster. She abandoned the temple to find the thieves and return the relic.",
